  "selectedText": "cell division",
  "surroundingContext": "Cell division is the process by which one parent cell divides into two daughter cells. Before division is complete, the cell must copy its genetic material so each new cell receives the information it needs. The cell then separates its contents and forms two cells.\n\nThe best spatial representation is a timeline that the learner can scrub. Each stage should be visible as a beat: parent cell, DNA copying, separation, and two daughter cells. This is stronger than a static cell model because division is a process, not just an object.",
